# CUT OS environment
#
# Copy to .env.local and fill in from your Supabase project:
#   Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API

# Safe to expose to the browser. Row-level security is what actually protects
# your data, and it is keyed to the signed-in user.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Optional. Where Supabase should send the email-confirmation link back to.
# Set this in any deployment behind a proxy, where the request headers are not
# a reliable guide to the public URL. Whatever you use must also be listed
# under Authentication -> URL Configuration -> Redirect URLs in Supabase.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://cut-os.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HEVY (training)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER ONLY, and required for any Hevy sync. Get it from
# https://hevy.com/settings?developer - the API is a Hevy Pro feature.
#
# NEVER prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_: anything so prefixed is inlined into the
# browser bundle by Next.js. It is read only by lib/integrations/hevy/env.ts,
# which is server-only, and it is never stored in the database.
HEVY_API_KEY=your-hevy-api-key

# Optional. The API host is not stated in Hevy's published documentation, which
# gives paths and no origin, so the default was inferred rather than read. If
# "Test connection" on /import fails to reach Hevy at all, set this.
# HEVY_API_BASE_URL=https://api.hevyapp.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SCHEDULED SYNC (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# All three are needed together, and only for the hourly sync in vercel.json.
# The "Sync Hevy" button on /import needs none of them and works without any of
# this configured; with them unset, /api/hevy/sync answers 503 and changes
# nothing.
#
# Vercel sends CRON_SECRET as an Authorization: Bearer header on a cron request
# when the variable is set. The route compares it in constant time.
# CRON_SECRET=a-long-random-string

# SERVER ONLY. NEVER prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_. This key BYPASSES EVERY RLS
# POLICY, which is the boundary the rest of this application relies on, so it is
# needed only where there is no signed-in user to key those policies to - a
# scheduled request carries no cookie session. Exactly one file may import it
# (app/api/hevy/sync/route.ts), and a test fails the build if a second one does.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# The auth.users id the scheduled sync acts for. With no session there is no
# "current user", so it is named explicitly and every query on that path filters
# by it - because RLS is not there to catch a mistake. Find it in Supabase under
# Authentication -> Users.
# CUT_OS_OWNER_USER_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
